      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High-dose ibuprofen is generally not recommended without a doctor's prescription, as kidney stones can cause renal impairment and may increase the risk of kidney damage rather than simply relieve pain. Even if you manage the pain with medication, passing a stone requires monitoring for infection or blockage which a simple home approach cannot address. Please contact your urologist or an urgent care clinic tonight for a proper assessment and safe pain management plan instead of waiting until the next morning.",
      "source": "target",
